Runway 14/32 is the primary runway, handling all commercial passenger operations. Runway 14R/32L, added in 1996, is used for domestic services, general aviation, flight training, and as a relief runway during peak periods. Both runways are equipped with [[Instrument Landing System|ILS]] Category I approach systems.

=== Cargo facilities ===

Portnou International Airport has dedicated cargo facilities on the western side of the airport, adjacent to Runway 14R/32L, with a cargo apron, warehousing, and handling facilities operated by the [[Balboa Airports Authority]]. The cargo facilities serve the airport's role as a freight gateway for the [[Portnou]] port complex — the [[Balboa Canal|canal]]'s Shendan terminus — linking sea freight transshipment with air cargo connections to the Lurandian and Abyalan regions. The airport handled 48,000 tonnes of cargo in 2025. [[Transabyala AirFreight]], a dedicated cargo airline, is based at the airport and operates freighter services to destinations across Lurandia and Abyala from the cargo apron.

