== Ground transport ==

=== Rail ===

[[File:Portnou International Airport CristoCarril station.png|thumb|250px|The CristoCarril station at Portnou International Airport]]
<!-- Image prompt: A commuter rail station at a tropical regional airport. A modern covered platform with a CristoCarril commuter train stopped at the platform, passengers boarding. Airport terminal visible in the background beyond the tracks. Palm trees, tropical light, warm atmosphere. -->

The airport is served by [[CristoCarril]] [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]], which runs on the Coastal Line corridor between the [[Estació Central de Portnou]] and [[Barcelona Main Station]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The airport station, '''[[Aeroport de Portnou]]''', is located adjacent to the terminal, with a covered walkway connecting the platform to the check-in area. Line A provides the only CristoCarril stop in [[Les Drassanes]]; the other stations in the municipality are served by [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 1. Journey time to the Estació Central de Portnou is approximately 15 minutes, and to Barcelona Main Station approximately 85 minutes.

=== Road ===

The airport is connected to the regional road network via the [[E21 (Balboa)|E21]] expressway, which runs from the port area of Portnou through the northwestern suburbs to the airport and onward to [[Barcelona (ciutat)|Barcelona]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]]. Journey time by road to central Portnou is approximately 20–30 minutes depending on traffic. Taxi, ride-hailing, and private vehicle access is available at the terminal. Short-term and long-term parking is provided in a surface car park adjacent to the terminal.

=== Bus ===

The municipal bus network operates an airport express route connecting the airport to the [[Estació Central de Portnou]] and the city centre, with intermediate stops at the major rail stations along the E21 corridor. The service complements the CristoCarril connection and provides an alternative for passengers travelling from neighbourhoods not served by the rail line.

